warning[R0312] (conservative): `for` loop at module scope
--> 9:1: runs when the module is first required
  = note: a module's top level runs on the first `require`, before the requirer gets anything back: work there delays every requirer, and nothing declares its order
  = note: calls inside the loop are not reported one by one
  = note: valid Luau: whether a module may loop as it loads is this project's choice (`allow-loops` under `[rules.module-scope-computation]` in rime.toml)
  = help: move the loop into a function, so it runs when something calls it

